直接从挡风玻璃上飞起来了！
lifts itself
clean off the screen!

402
00:20:48,167 --> 00:20:49,700
这下好了。
There you go.

403
00:20:49,733 --> 00:20:54,667
我瞎了！
我彻底瞎了！
I'm blind!
I'm completely blind!

404
00:20:54,667 --> 00:20:57,400
厂家说这辆车
在高速行驶时更稳了，
They say this car
is more stable at high speeds,

405
00:20:57,433 --> 00:21:01,767
转向变迟钝些之后，
过弯时也没那么神经质了。
and that lazier steering
has made it less nervous
in the bends.

406
00:21:02,167 --> 00:21:03,667
呵，鬼才信！
Yeah, right!

407
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:10,900
我觉得，你要是全神贯注去开，
它确实比老款Tuscan
I suppose if you really
concentrate it is a little
bit less nervous

408
00:21:12,833 --> 00:21:17,500
少了一点点神经质，
但它依然像一匹盎格鲁-阿拉伯烈马。
than the old Tuscan,
but it's still like
an Anglo-Arab horse.

409
00:21:17,533 --> 00:21:20,533
连续二十年每天路过同一个井盖都相安无事，
Goes past the same drain cover
every day for 20 years,

410
00:21:20,567 --> 00:21:22,667
然后突然有一天，“哇啊！”受惊了！
and then one day, "Whoa!"

411
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:28,167
哎哟喂！
我们在原地转圈圈呢。
Hello!
We're going round in circles.

412
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,800
（大笑）
(LAUGHS)

413
00:21:32,067 --> 00:21:34,333
真是辆疯子车。
What an insane car.

414
00:21:34,367 --> 00:21:36,667
所以，这车绝对不好开。
So, it's not
an easy car to drive.

415
00:21:36,667 --> 00:21:40,367
但日常用起来
会不会稍微省心点呢？
But is it now
an easier car
to live with?

416
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:43,500
为了找出答案，
我把隔壁赛道工厂里的
To find out,
I have assembled
a group of guys

417
00:21:43,533 --> 00:21:46,500
这群哥们儿找了过来。
from this factory
which is next to our track.

418
00:21:46,533 --> 00:21:50,667
你们当中谁能第一个
I will offer 20 quid
to the first one of you

419
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:53,900
跑到那辆车前、钻进去、
that can get to that car,
get in it,

420
00:21:53,933 --> 00:21:58,667
打着引擎再下车，
而且在一分钟内搞定，我就赏他20镑！
start the engine, get out,
in under a minute.

421
00:21:58,667 --> 00:22:01,100
这是车钥匙。
计时开始！
These are the keys.
Your time starts now.

422
00:22:01,133 --> 00:22:04,567
门已经开了，不用管锁。
直接钻进去就行。
It's already open,
so don't worry about that.
Just get in.

423
00:22:04,667 --> 00:22:07,033
加油啊哥们儿。啊！
Come on, man. Ah!

424
00:22:08,033 --> 00:22:09,567
这小伙行啊，手脚真麻利。
He's good. He's very good.

425
00:22:09,667 --> 00:22:12,467
他只用了十秒就坐进去了。
It only took him ten seconds
to get in.

426
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:15,500
已经过去30秒了。
30 seconds has gone.

427
00:22:16,133 --> 00:22:18,467
三、二、一！
Three, two, one!

428
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:20,100
彻底失败！
Total failure!

429
00:22:20,133 --> 00:22:21,667
好了，
麻烦您出来吧。
Right,
if you wanna step out.

430
00:22:22,733 --> 00:22:25,800
快点，乔，赶紧下车。
Come on, Joe, out the car.

431
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:29,100
劳驾赶紧出来成吗，
后面还有人排队试呢，而且天都下雪了。
If you could just get out,
we've got others to try,
and it's snowing.

432
00:22:29,133 --> 00:22:31,133
还得我放你出来！
I'll have to let you out!

433
00:22:31,167 --> 00:22:32,833
好了。出来吧。
Now. There you go.

434
00:22:32,867 --> 00:22:34,067
这表现让我刮目相看。
I'm impressed.

435
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:37,233
哎哟！哎呀天哪，不行。
Oh! Oh dear, no.

436
00:22:37,267 --> 00:22:39,700
很遗憾，你时间到了。
I'm sorry , your time is up.

437
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:42,467
劳驾现在下车吧，谢谢。
If you'd like to
step out now, please.

438
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,500
大妹子，你从那儿可钻不出来。
You'll not get
through there, love.

439
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:49,933
已经过去25秒了。
25 seconds has now gone.

440
00:22:49,967 --> 00:22:53,667
他居然把收音机打开了！
他去捣鼓那该死的收音机了！
He's turned on the radio!
He's gone for the damn radio.

441
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:57,000
快点儿。
后头还有好几个
得测呢。
Come on.
We've got some more
to go through.

442
00:22:57,033 --> 00:23:00,667
我的天呐。
又有一个出不来的。
Oh, my God.
Another one can't get out.

443
00:23:00,667 --> 00:23:02,833
所以要是有偷车贼
正在看节目，
So if you're a car thief
watching this,

444
00:23:02,867 --> 00:23:06,267
在路边看到这玩意儿，趁早死心吧！
see one of these on the side
of the street ,forget it!

445
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:08,933
那是喇叭！
这个是目前最惨不忍睹的。
That's the horn!
This is the worst yet.

446
00:23:08,967 --> 00:23:12,700
钻进去动作最快，
然后就干坐了
整整53秒。
Fastest in,
and then 53 seconds
of just sitting there.

447
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:17,667
这位是马克。
他是这家工厂的老大。
This is Mark.
He's the boss of the factory.

448
00:23:17,667 --> 00:23:21,267
他靠着聪明才智
和老谋深算，
一路混上了这个位置。
He's worked his way up
using intelligence
and cunning.

449
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:25,667
他把车门给关上了，
很显然，
这绝对是个失策。
He's closed the door
which, of course,
is a mistake.

450
00:23:25,667 --> 00:23:27,700
还剩五秒，马克。
加把劲啊，你可是大老板，老兄！
Five seconds, Mark.
Come on, you're the boss, man!

451
00:23:27,733 --> 00:23:31,967
打个火总该会吧。
时间到！
You should be able
to start a car.
And your time is up!

452
00:23:33,333 --> 00:23:36,267
搞快点，马克，
我们后头可还有
一大堆镜头要拍呢。
Come on, Mark,
we've actually got quite a lot
more filming to do.

453
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:41,167
所以，答案显而易见。
日常开这车，
绝对能把你折腾疯。
So, there's the answer.
No, it's not an easy car
to live with.

454
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:45,667
而且现在，很显然，
它再也不能
在这个市场独霸天下了。
And now, of course,
it no longer
has the market to itself.

455
00:23:46,533 --> 00:23:48,567
那么哪台更好呢？
So which is best?

456
00:23:48,667 --> 00:23:53,000
是精密、考究、
冷静优雅的威兹曼，
The technical, exquisite
ice-cool Wiesmann,

457
00:23:53,033 --> 00:23:56,067
还是那台狂暴粗野、
胸毛炸裂的TVR？
or the mad,
hairy-chested TVR?

458
00:23:59,733 --> 00:24:03,967
是牙医的精密钻头，
还是暴力的打桩机？
The dentist's drill
or the pile-driver?

459
00:24:06,667 --> 00:24:08,533
好吧，
要是单论绝对极速，
Well,
in terms of outright speed,

460
00:24:08,567 --> 00:24:12,667
那台德国车跑到158英里
就黔驴技穷了，
the German car is all out
of ideas at 158,

461
00:24:12,667 --> 00:24:16,667
而那台“俄罗斯车”
能飙到180。
whereas the Russian car
can do 180.

462
00:24:16,667 --> 00:24:20,100
然后再看价格。
威兹曼要6万英镑，
Then there's price.
The Wiesmann is £60,000,

463
00:24:20,133 --> 00:24:24,933
而TVR只要3.9万英镑。
whereas the TVR is £39,000.

464
00:24:24,967 --> 00:24:29,233
所以TVR更快、
马力大得多、
而且便宜了一大截。
So the TVR is faster,
a lot more powerful
and much cheaper.

465
00:24:29,267 --> 00:24:33,167
听起来是一场碾压局。
但事情可没那么简单。
Sounds like a walkover.
But it's not that simple.

466
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:37,167
你看，
我老婆超爱这台车。
You see,
my wife loves this car.

467
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:40,667
她爱那轰鸣声、
那股震颤感，
还有命悬一线的刺激，
She loves the noise
and the vibrations
and the sense of danger

468
00:24:40,667 --> 00:24:43,167
以及只要一超转速，
and the way that
when you over-rev it,

469
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:48,967
整面仪表盘亮得
就跟狒狒的红屁股一模一样。
the whole dash lights up
like a baboon's backside.

470
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,933
但理查德·哈蒙德呢，
恰恰相反，
他恨死这车了。
Richard Hammond,
on the other hand,
he pretty much hates it.

471
00:24:52,967 --> 00:24:55,500
他说这车太难伺候、
繁琐得要命，
He says it's too difficult
and too complicated,

472
00:24:55,533 --> 00:25:00,167
而且里头的缝线，
看着就像那种……
and that all the stitching
in here looks like the
kind of stitching you find

473
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:02,800
自己笨手笨脚
补鞋缝出来的针脚。
when someone's tried to
mend their own shoes.

474
00:25:04,700 --> 00:25:06,400
所以说，这是一台“马麦酱”车。
It's a Marmite car, then.

475
00:25:06,433 --> 00:25:08,833
你要是爱它，
别的车连看都不想看。
If you love it,
nothing else will do.

476
00:25:08,867 --> 00:25:12,500
没有任何东西能给你
带来哪怕一丝这种快感。
Nothing else offers you
anything like the thrill.

477
00:25:14,767 --> 00:25:17,467
但你要是讨厌它，
也别慌，
But if you hate it,
don't worry,

478
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:19,667
因为你
还有别的选择。
because there
is an alternative.

479
00:25:22,933 --> 00:25:24,233
（现场观众鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDS)

480
00:25:24,267 --> 00:25:26,167
拍得真棒。
~ 是啊，漂亮极了。
Lovely pictures.
Yeah, beautiful.

481
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:29,700
-一天之内把各种天气全赶上了。
-样样齐活。
-Every single weather
in one day.
-The whole lot.

482
00:25:29,733 --> 00:25:33,667
现在有个关键问题，
你干嘛这么讨厌TVR？
Now, big question,
why do you hate TVRs so much?

483
00:25:33,667 --> 00:25:35,767
我干嘛讨厌TVR？
因为首先一点，
Why do I hate TVRs?
Because for one thing,

484
00:25:35,800 --> 00:25:39,333
它们全是用塑料和玻璃纤维拼出来的，
闻起来像皮划艇制造厂。
they're all made of plastic
and fibreglass, and they smell
like canoe factories.

485
00:25:39,367 --> 00:25:41,533
到处都挂着没刮干净的胶水渣，
You got bits
of glue hanging off
all over the place,

486
00:25:41,567 --> 00:25:43,367
橡胶密封胶条动不动就脱落。
all the rubber trim falls off.

487
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:47,100
其中有些车，
你要是摇下侧车窗，
后挡风玻璃能直接被气流掀飞。
On some of them,
if you open the side windows
the back window blows out.

488
00:25:47,133 --> 00:25:49,733
但问题是，
它们现在可比以前好多了。
The thing is,
they are a lot better
than they used to be.

489
00:25:49,767 --> 00:25:51,233
我以前其实开过其中一辆。
I actually had one of these.

490
00:25:51,267 --> 00:25:54,167
-说实话，我觉得测的就是眼前这辆。
-是吗？
-In fact, I think it was
that one on test.
-Yeah?

491
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,467
结果它根本打不着火。
And it wouldn't start.

492
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:57,400
是打不着火，
还是你不会打火？
Wouldn't start
or you couldn't start it?

493
00:25:57,433 --> 00:26:00,100
不是，绝不可能！
我正经上过课，
翻过说明书，还看过教学录像。
No, no, no, no!
I'd had the lesson,
read the book, seen the video.

494
00:26:00,133 --> 00:26:03,233
这一套我都门儿清。
我知道怎么打火，
但它就是坏了。
All of that.
I knew how to start it,
but it broke down.

495
00:26:03,267 --> 00:26:07,300
正因如此，
我宁愿选那辆威兹曼（Wiesmann）。
All of that is why I would
rather have the Wiesmann.

496
00:26:07,333 --> 00:26:09,433
-真的。
-那可贵了足足两万一千英镑！
-I would.
-£21,000 more.

497
00:26:09,467 --> 00:26:10,800
对，我知道，
是贵了一大笔钱，
Yes, I know,
it's a lot more money,

498
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:13,400
但就算这样，
我还是更想要那辆。
but still,
I would rather have that.

499
00:26:13,433 --> 00:26:15,867
你猜怎么着？
我挺你。
Do you know what?
I'm with you.

500
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:17,900
我也选它。我也选它。
So would I. So would I.

501
00:26:17,933 --> 00:26:20,033
不过当然了，咱们还有最重要的测试要做。
But of course, we do have
the important test to do.

502
00:26:20,067 --> 00:26:24,133
我们必须把这两辆车交给咱们的驯养赛车手。
We must hand them both over
to our tame racing driver.

503
00:26:24,167 --> 00:26:27,967
有人说，
他的头像被印在瑞典的高面值邮票上；
Some say that
he appears on high-value
stamps in Sweden,

504
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:30,700
还有人说他能用舌头逮鱼。
and he can catch fish
with his tongue.

505
00:26:30,733 --> 00:26:33,733
我们只知道他叫——斯提格（The Stig）。
We know him only as the Stig.

506
00:26:33,767 --> 00:26:36,367
克拉克森：先测TVR，他出发了！
CLARKSON: So, TVR first,
and away he goes!

507
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:40,400
350匹暴躁的俄罗斯烈马瞬间弹射起步。
350 angry Russian horses
kicking it off the line.

508
00:26:40,433 --> 00:26:43,667
逼近一号弯，
这对斯提格来说绝对是一场狂暴颠簸的挑战！
Up to the first corner,
this is gonna be a wild ride
for the Stig!

509
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:47,800
你已经能看到他在死命跟方向盘较劲，
把这辆Tuscan摁在赛道上！
Already you can see him
fighting to keep the Tuscan
on the track!

510
00:26:50,467 --> 00:26:54,467
带感。里面放的是里克·韦克曼和Yes乐队的多重合成器曲风。
Nice. The multi-synth stylings
of Rick Wakeman and Yes there.

511
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:57,967
那是《Yours Is No Disgrace》（这绝非耻辱），
但眼下这圈成绩会是耻辱吗？
That's Yours Is No Disgrace.
But is this?

512
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,133
他过芝加哥弯（Chicago）竟然出奇地干净利落。
He's surprisingly tidy
round Chicago there.

513
00:27:00,167 --> 00:27:03,000
真正的考验来了，
是锤头弯（Hammerhead）。
它会转向不足吗？
Here comes the real test,
it's the Hammerhead.
Will it understeer?

514
00:27:03,033 --> 00:27:06,800
是会转向过度，
还是干脆彻底失去转向？
Will it oversteer,
or simply fail to
steer at all?

515
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:09,900
车屁股正蠢蠢欲动想甩出去，
但在斯提格手里，门儿都没有！
The back end's
trying to break loose,
not on Stig's watch.

516
00:27:11,567 --> 00:27:13,533
好，杀入穿心弯（Followthrough）。
Okay, down to
the Followthrough.

517
00:27:14,367 --> 00:27:15,900
看着可真快。
That looks fast.

518
00:27:15,933 --> 00:27:19,933
同时也险象环生。
只剩最后两个弯了！
Also rather hairy.
There's only two more
corners to go!

519
00:27:19,967 --> 00:27:22,900
倒数第二个弯，
他现在绝对不能失控打转。
It's the second-last corner.
He can't afford
to lose it now.

520
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:26,200
死死咬在极限边缘杀入甘邦弯（Gambon），
冲线！
Right on the edge
into Gambon
and across the line!

521
00:27:26,233 --> 00:27:28,667
现在，轮到威兹曼登场了。
And now, it's the Wiesmann.

522
00:27:28,667 --> 00:27:31,700
伴着极具德国风范的严谨打滑，
他冲出去了。
Off he goes with some
precise German wheel spin.

523
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:34,233
忍不住让人觉得，
斯提格开这车会轻松不少，
Can't help thinking
the Stig will have
an easier time here,

524
00:27:34,267 --> 00:27:36,833
但圈速能更快吗？
but will it be
a quicker time?

525
00:27:36,867 --> 00:27:38,400
进第一个弯看着相当稳当。
He's looking controlled
in the first corner.

526
00:27:38,433 --> 00:27:42,967
那套扁平比极薄极薄的轮胎，
发出了一点尖叫。
Bit of squeal from those
very, very low-profile tyres.

527
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:46,300
过芝加哥弯。
TVR在这表现不错，那威兹曼呢？
Through Chicago.
TVR was good here,
and the Wiesmann?

528
00:27:46,333 --> 00:27:47,667
其实还要更好。
Even better, actually.

529
00:27:47,667 --> 00:27:49,467
出弯时屁股只是轻轻扭了一下。
Just a little hip wiggle
on the way out.

530
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:52,667
进锤头弯看着挺快。
车头开始推头走宽了。
Hammerhead looking fast
on the way in.
Nose starts to run wide.

531
00:27:52,700 --> 00:27:55,767
斯提格用一记漂亮可控的滑移
救了回来。
Stig cancels it out with
lovely controlled slide.

532
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,067
噢，太帅了。
现在进入贯通弯。
Oh, that is beautiful.
Now, Followthrough.

533
00:27:58,100 --> 00:28:00,533
大油门顶着，姿态不错。
Keeping the power on,
