当时搞了场
媒体群访，
and they did
a press pack interview

653
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:52,833
就在洛杉矶的片场。
on the set in Los Angeles.

654
00:33:52,867 --> 00:33:55,733
那个记者问我：
“你平时开什么车？”
And the guy said to me,
"What car do you drive?"

655
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:57,100
我说：“我不会开车。”
And I said, "I don't drive."

656
00:33:57,133 --> 00:33:58,833
但我一跟那家伙
说我不会开车，
But when told this guy
that I didn't drive,

657
00:33:58,867 --> 00:34:01,000
他整个人居然
下意识地往后退。
he actually physically
backed away from me.

658
00:34:01,033 --> 00:34:03,367
这种待遇
我这辈子见得多了。
Which is what
I've experienced all my life.

659
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:06,500
那你开车之前是怎么过的？
我是说，你平时怎么出行啊？
What did you do
before you were driving then?
I mean, how did you get about?

660
00:34:06,533 --> 00:34:09,833
呃，当年……也就是在
我本该学开车的年纪，
Well, I lived in... The time
when I would have been
learning to drive,

661
00:34:09,867 --> 00:34:11,567
在我老爸本该
教我开车的时候，
when me old fella
would have taught me to drive,

662
00:34:11,667 --> 00:34:13,267
就是他教我几个兄弟开车那会儿，
this time
when he taught me brothers,

663
00:34:13,300 --> 00:34:14,733
我还在伦敦念大学呢。
I was living in London
as a student.

664
00:34:14,767 --> 00:34:17,033
而且我想找的工作
全都在伦敦。
All the work I was after
was in London.

665
00:34:17,067 --> 00:34:18,867
去哪儿我都靠走，靠跑。
I walked. Ran everywhere.

666
00:34:18,900 --> 00:34:21,100
-啥？
-我是个马拉松跑者，
我跑马拉松的。
-What?
-I'm a marathoner.
I run marathons.

667
00:34:21,133 --> 00:34:22,867
-你是个马拉松跑者？
-对啊。
-You're a marathon runner?
-Yeah.

668
00:34:22,900 --> 00:34:24,467
这可不明智。
That's not sensible.

669
00:34:24,500 --> 00:34:26,400
-（全场大笑）
-我是说，要是得走完26英里，
-(ALL LAUGHING)
-I mean, if you've
gotta cover 26 miles,

670
00:34:26,433 --> 00:34:28,033
开车明智多了好嘛。
you are better off driving.

671
00:34:29,200 --> 00:34:30,533
那我向你下战书。
Well, I'll challenge you.

672
00:34:30,567 --> 00:34:32,300
-什么？
-我要挑战你。
-What?
-I'll challenge you.

673
00:34:32,333 --> 00:34:34,000
-你……
-我用跑的，你开车。
-You...
-I'll run it, you drive it.

674
00:34:37,467 --> 00:34:39,367
我说真的，
你倒是给我出了个好主意。
I tell you what,
you've given me an idea.

675
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:43,167
要是咱们办一场比赛……
就按伦敦马拉松的路线，行吧？
If we stage a race...
The London Marathon
course, okay?

676
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:46,000
找个人靠双腿跑，
然后我开着车跟他比。
Someone can run it,
and then I'll race them
in a car.

677
00:34:46,033 --> 00:34:48,567
就选个普通的周中工作日早晨。
Normal week day morning.

678
00:34:48,667 --> 00:34:51,000
我觉得车能赢。
你觉得呢，车赢还是人赢？
I reckon the car.
What do you reckon,
car or runner?

679
00:34:51,033 --> 00:34:53,433
-我押跑步的赢，嗯。
-你押跑步的？
-I'd back the runner. Mmm.
-You'd back the runner?

680
00:34:53,467 --> 00:34:55,133
-要是我去跑呢？
-毕竟路上那么堵。
-What if I ran it?
-With the traffic.

681
00:34:55,167 --> 00:34:56,800
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

682
00:34:56,833 --> 00:34:59,667
我曾经……
我曾经跑过26米。
I have once...
I once ran 26 metres.

683
00:34:59,700 --> 00:35:01,367
-天哪，疼死我了。
-（全场大笑）
-God, it hurt.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

684
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:05,900
行了，听着。
你穿梭过时空，对吧？
Anyway, listen.
You've travelled across
space and time, okay?

685
00:35:05,933 --> 00:35:07,933
你打过戴立克，
拯救过全宇宙。
You've fought Daleks.
You've saved the universe.

686
00:35:07,967 --> 00:35:10,667
-但现在，轮到你
有史以来最大的挑战了。
-嗯。
-But now, it's time for your
biggest ever challenge.
-Hmm.

687
00:35:10,700 --> 00:35:13,967
-你得开着那台Liana
跑完我们的赛道。
-（全场大笑）
-You've got to get
the Liana round our track.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

688
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:17,533
不过有个棘手的问题，
因为你说过
你绝不上这节目，
However, there was one problem
because you said
you wouldn't come on the show

689
00:35:17,567 --> 00:35:20,000
-要是逼你开
我们那台普通手动挡Liana的话。
-没错。
-if you have to drive
our normal Liana.
-That's right.

690
00:35:20,033 --> 00:35:21,333
因为……
Because...

691
00:35:21,367 --> 00:35:25,100
因为我考的驾照
只能开自动挡。
Because I'm only qualified
to drive an automatic.

692
00:35:25,133 --> 00:35:26,833
-堂堂神秘博士啊！
-（全场大笑）
-Doctor Who.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

693
00:35:27,900 --> 00:35:29,800
-神秘博士哎！
-我现在就等着
你们全都吓得往后躲，
-Doctor Who.
-Now I expect
you all to back away

694
00:35:29,833 --> 00:35:32,233
搞得我像得了什么瘟疫似的。
like I've got some disease.

695
00:35:32,267 --> 00:35:34,833
我是说，你们当时还说：
“哎呀，我们给你安排
几堂课练练嘛。”
I mean, I think what you said,
"Oh, we'll give you
a few lessons."

696
00:35:34,867 --> 00:35:36,667
我心想：
“得了吧，我闭着眼都能想到！”
And I thought,
"Yeah, I can see that!"

697
00:35:36,700 --> 00:35:38,467
在全国电视观众面前
丢人现眼。
Going out
on national television.

698
00:35:38,500 --> 00:35:41,667
-看我练手动挡的糗相，
天哪，惨不忍睹。
-（模仿打齿熄火声）
-My lessons in a manual.
Oh, terrible.
-(IMITATING GEARS FAULTERING)

699
00:35:41,667 --> 00:35:43,800
我根本就不是
开车的料，一点天分都没有。
I am not a natural driver
in any way.

700
00:35:43,833 --> 00:35:45,667
行，待会儿我们就能见分晓了。
不过嘛……
Well, we're gonna
find that out in a minute.
But, there's...

701
00:35:45,700 --> 00:35:46,833
我只是觉得
得先把预防针打在前头。
I just thought
I'd get that in early.

702
00:35:46,867 --> 00:35:48,667
-好吧，铺垫得不错。
-（全场大笑）
-Yeah. Nice try.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

703
00:35:48,667 --> 00:35:52,167
你知道全英国一共有多少辆
自动挡的铃木Liana吗？
Do you know how many
automatic Suzuki Lianas
there are in Britain?

704
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:54,433
全国路上跑着3100万辆车。
31 million vehicles
on the road.

705
00:35:54,467 --> 00:35:57,067
其中整整40辆，
是自动挡Liana。
40 of them,
are Liana automatics.

706
00:35:57,100 --> 00:36:00,833
所以我们得满英国掘地三尺找出一辆，
再运到这儿来。
So, we had to find
one of these cars in Britain
and get it down here.

707
00:36:00,867 --> 00:36:02,967
这么说，你们节目之前
就没人开过自动挡？
So, you had nobody
else on this show
whose driven an automatic?

708
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,233
没有，他们开的全是同一辆手动挡。
No. They've all driven
the same manual car.

709
00:36:05,267 --> 00:36:06,433
看来我很特别嘛。
So, I'm special.

710
00:36:06,467 --> 00:36:08,300
我们这辆还是
跟别人借来的。
We had to borrow this
from somebody.

711
00:36:08,333 --> 00:36:11,000
我也不知道是从哪儿搞来的，
反正是一辆借来的车。
I don't know
where we've got it from,
but it's a borrowed car.

712
00:36:11,033 --> 00:36:12,267
-嗯哼。
-不是我们的车。
-Mmm-hmm.
-It's not ours.

713
00:36:12,300 --> 00:36:14,233
那么，有谁想看
他是怎么“糟蹋”它的？
And who would like to see
how he treated it?

714
00:36:14,267 --> 00:36:15,667
我觉得原车主看到之后不会太高兴，
I don't think
they'll be too happy,

715
00:36:15,667 --> 00:36:16,800
-当他们拿回车的时候。
-咱们直接看大屏幕吧。
-when they get it back.
-Let's just have a look.

716
00:36:16,833 --> 00:36:19,267
有请克里斯托弗
开着借来的Liana登场！
Here is Christopher
in a borrowed Liana.

717
00:36:19,300 --> 00:36:20,900
-然后……噢！
-这段我还没看过呢。
-And... Oh!
-I've not seen this.

718
00:36:20,933 --> 00:36:23,267
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-克拉克森：冲出去啦！
-(SCREECHING)
-CLARKSON: There he goes!

719
00:36:23,300 --> 00:36:24,667
（埃克莱斯顿大笑）
(ECCLESTON LAUGHS)

720
00:36:24,667 --> 00:36:26,667
克拉克森：刚才那是……
那是头一回打转。
CLARKSON: That was...
That was one.

721
00:36:26,667 --> 00:36:29,033
这又来了一次，
瞧，他又杀过来了。
This is another one,
here he comes again.

722
00:36:29,067 --> 00:36:31,833
噢，这次甩到那边去了。
而且他又来了！
Oh, back that way that time.
And here he comes again!

723
00:36:31,867 --> 00:36:33,667
（轮胎尖叫声）
(SCREECHING)

724
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:36,300
所以要那是你的车，自认倒霉吧！
So if that's your car, tough!

725
00:36:36,333 --> 00:36:37,933
额，总之。
Um, anyway.

726
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:41,167
-谁想看看
这之后跑的那一圈？
-全场：想！
-Who'd like to see
the lap that followed that?
-ALL: Yeah!

727
00:36:41,200 --> 00:36:42,667
-你想看吗？
-太想看了。
-Do you wanna see this?
-I'd love to.

728
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:44,533
行，放录像。
咱们来瞧瞧。
All right, play the tape.
Let's have a look.

729
00:36:44,567 --> 00:36:46,000
（呼啸声）
(WHOOSHING)

730
00:36:47,767 --> 00:36:50,033
我坐出租车过来那会儿就预料到了。
I predicted that
in the taxi down.

731
00:36:50,067 --> 00:36:51,700
克拉克森：没错。
CLARKSON: Yes.

732
00:36:51,733 --> 00:36:56,000
有种塔迪斯时光机的感觉。
好，要开始了。
It's that TARDIS feel to it.
And here we go.

733
00:36:56,033 --> 00:36:58,833
刚才那几把打转没把你吓着吧？
Were you a bit unnerved
by the spins?

734
00:36:58,867 --> 00:37:03,667
埃克莱斯顿：倒没有……
身体上倒没觉得害怕，我只是……
ECCLESTON: I wasn't...
I was never physically scared,
I was just...

735
00:37:03,667 --> 00:37:06,667
我只是魔怔了似的想把它开明白。
I was obsessed
with trying to master it.

736
00:37:06,700 --> 00:37:08,467
克拉克森：不得不说，
这跑得看着挺像样。
CLARKSON: This is
looking good,
I have to say.

737
00:37:08,500 --> 00:37:10,900
你这会儿绝对是全神贯注了。
You're certainly
concentrating there.

738
00:37:10,933 --> 00:37:12,833
好，这里得慢点进。
Now, slow in here.

739
00:37:12,867 --> 00:37:15,933
嗯……依我看，
进主跑道那会儿速度可能有点太快了。
Mmm. I'd say
it's probably a bit too fast
going in to that runway.

740
00:37:15,967 --> 00:37:19,200
-这个弯……锤头弯过得怎么样？还行吧？
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-This one... How was
the Hammerhead there? Good?
-(SCREECHING)

741
00:37:22,133 --> 00:37:23,567
漂亮。
Good.

742
00:37:23,667 --> 00:37:27,433
我在想，
要是我的思维转得更快，车会不会也更快。
I'm wondering,
if I think faster,
I'll go faster.

743
00:37:27,467 --> 00:37:30,967
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-埃克莱斯顿：噢，我的天哪！
-(SCREECHING)
-ECCLESTON: Oh, Jesus!

744
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:33,967
对一个驾龄
才区区14个月的人来说，
This for someone
who's only been
driving 14 months

745
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:36,333
这表现相当厉害了。
is quite impressive.

746
00:37:36,367 --> 00:37:38,733
埃克莱斯顿：这就是……
对，看这儿。
ECCLESTON: This was...
Yeah, here we go.

747
00:37:38,767 --> 00:37:40,767
克拉克森：噢！又冲出去了！
CLARKSON: Oh! Off again!

748
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,367
埃克莱斯顿：那是甘邦弯吗？
ECCLESTON: Is that
Gambon corner?

749
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:43,967
克拉克森：不，
这个才是甘邦弯。
CLARKSON: No,
this is Gambon corner.

750
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:46,400
内侧直接切上了路肩，差点整台车给翻了。
He hit the kerb on the inside
and nearly rolled it over.

751
00:37:46,433 --> 00:37:49,900
-到了，冲线！
-（全场鼓掌）
-There you are,
across the line!
-(ALL APPLAUDING)

752
00:37:56,300 --> 00:38:00,433
-其实你冲线的时候
已经是1936年了。
-（笑声）
-You did actually
cross the line in 1936.
-(LAUGHS)

753
00:38:00,467 --> 00:38:02,133
这就是当时间领主的优势嘛。
It's the advantage
of being a Time Lord.

754
00:38:02,167 --> 00:38:05,867
那你当时觉得斯提格就像外星球来的怪物吗？
Did you think the Stig
was like someone
from planet Zarg then?

755
00:38:05,900 --> 00:38:07,500
他其实……
他是个特别棒的教练。
He was...
He's a great teacher.

756
00:38:07,533 --> 00:38:08,767
他算好教练？
He's a good teacher?

757
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:11,400
我开的时候一点都没慌，我只是觉得……
I never panicked doing it,
I just thought...

758
00:38:11,433 --> 00:38:13,300
人家那么卖力地想教好我，
He's tried so hard
to teach me well,

759
00:38:13,333 --> 00:38:15,933
我心想：“我可得给他好好争口气。”
I thought, "I've gotta
do this right for him."

760
00:38:15,967 --> 00:38:17,267
然后转头就打了个转甩出去了。
And promptly spun off.

761
00:38:17,300 --> 00:38:18,933
-没错。
-（全场大笑）
-Yes.
-(ALL LAUGHING)

762
00:38:18,967 --> 00:38:21,733
反正我不管，
我觉得你这圈
跑得相当惊艳。
Well, I don't care.
I thought that was
a very impressive lap.

763
00:38:21,767 --> 00:38:26,300
那你觉得自己能排在
这块圈速榜的什么位置？
So where do you think
you've come on this board?

764
00:38:26,333 --> 00:38:29,900
我估计能排在……之上吧。
I reckon just above...

765
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:32,933
-在谁之上？
-特里尼和
迈克尔·甘本之间。
-Just above?
-Between Trinny
and Michael Gambon.

766
00:38:32,967 --> 00:38:34,800
我的天呐，那可……
他们在哪儿呢？
Oh, my word. That's...
Where are they?

767
00:38:34,833 --> 00:38:38,033
甘本在这儿，1分55秒。
没那么差，你跑得
比这好多了。
There's Gambon, 55.
No. You did a lot
better than that.

768
00:38:38,067 --> 00:38:39,400
-噢，是吗？
-对。
-Oh, did I?
-Yeah.

769
00:38:39,433 --> 00:38:41,833
你其实……
考虑到你算是……
You actually...
Bearing in mind
you're sort of...

770
00:38:41,867 --> 00:38:43,100
我赢了维尼！
I beat Vinnie!

771
00:38:43,133 --> 00:38:46,833
你跑赢了维尼·琼斯。
你的成绩是1分52秒4！
You've beaten Vinnie.
You did it in 1:52.4!

772
00:38:46,867 --> 00:38:49,433
-（全场鼓掌）
-那么，女士们先生们。
-(ALL APPLAUDING)
-So, Ladies and gentlemen.

773
00:38:51,667 --> 00:38:54,467
-你上榜了。
-我可算松了口气！
-You're in there.
-I'm so relieved!

774
00:38:56,133 --> 00:38:59,033
真是谢天谢地。
I'm so relieved.

775
00:38:59,067 --> 00:39:02,100
-那就好，确实。
-这是我见过你
笑得最舒心的一次。
-I'm glad. Yep.
-That's the most pleased
I've seen you look.

776
00:39:02,133 --> 00:39:03,667
看到没有？
每周都是这副德行。
Do you see?
It's the same every week.

777
00:39:03,700 --> 00:39:05,467
每个人来之前都说：
“我其实不在乎成绩。”
Everyone that comes says,
"I'm not that bothered."

778
00:39:05,500 --> 00:39:07,833
结果一到揭晓成绩，
所有人身子全往前倾，
When the time's coming,
everybody leans forward

779
00:39:07,867 --> 00:39:09,533
满脸都是：“我跑了多少？
我成绩到底是多少？”
like, "What did I do?
What did I do?"

780
00:39:09,567 --> 00:39:10,833
没有，我今天玩得很开心。
No, I had a great day.

781
00:39:10,867 --> 00:39:12,767
真的开得非常过瘾。
不过就像我刚才说的，
I've really enjoyed doing it.
But like I said,

782
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:14,933
当你真正握上方向盘，
你就会想做到极致。
when you're
actually doing it,
you wanna get it right.

783
00:39:14,967 --> 00:39:16,233
-跟干别的事一模一样。
-确实如此。
-It's like anything else.
-You do.

784
00:39:16,267 --> 00:39:17,767
就跟演戏或者去任何地方一样。
It's like playing the part
or wherever you go.

785
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:19,067
心里想着“行，我一定要彻底拿下”，
"Right, I'm gonna
master this,"

786
00:39:19,100 --> 00:39:20,900
然后一转眼
就已经跑完了。
and then suddenly
it's all over.

787
00:39:20,933 --> 00:39:22,967
反正你比维尼拿捏得好，
这才是最重要的。
Well, you've mastered it
more than Vinnie.
That's the important thing.

788
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,900
-女士们先生们，
克里斯托弗·埃克莱斯顿！
-（全场鼓掌）
-Ladies and gentlemen,
Christopher Eccleston!
-(ALL APPLAUDING)

789
00:39:25,933 --> 00:39:28,133
-太精彩了。
-谢谢。
-That was so brilliant.
-Thank you.

790
00:39:32,867 --> 00:39:34,667
好了！言归正传！
Right! Now!

791
00:39:34,700 --> 00:39:36,567
刚才，
杰里米开着
Earlier on,
Jeremy was ripping about

792
00:39:36,667 --> 00:39:39,000
两辆老派英国跑车
在赛道上撒欢狂飙。
a couple of old-fashioned
British sports cars.

793
00:39:39,033 --> 00:39:42,033
而我觉得，
是时候来点
更现代的狠货了。
And I thought
it was time for something
a bit more modern.

794
00:39:42,067 --> 00:39:43,733
（钢琴配乐）
(INSTRUMENTAL PIANO MUSIC)

795
00:39:46,733 --> 00:39:50,667
哈蒙德：阿斯顿·马丁DB9
颜值向来无可挑剔。
HAMMOND: The Aston Martin DB9
has always looked pretty.

796
00:39:53,533 --> 00:39:56,700
而现在，它变得更加惊艳绝伦了。
And now, it just got
a whole lot prettier.

797
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:06,267
这就是DB9 Volante。
This is the DB9 Volante.

798
00:40:06,300 --> 00:40:09,633
再好好多看两眼吧，
我先闭嘴安静一会儿。
Just have another look at it.
I'll stop talking for a bit.

799
00:40:20,600 --> 00:40:23,700
上一次
我们在节目里介绍DB9，
还是硬顶版，
The last time
we featured a DB9,
it was the hardtop

800
00:40:23,733 --> 00:40:26,300
当时杰里米开着它
一路狂飙到了法国南部
and Jeremy raced it
to the south of France

801
00:40:26,333 --> 00:40:29,700
跟坐火车的我和詹姆斯较量。
against James and me
on a train.

802
00:40:29,733 --> 00:40:32,000
